  "description": "This proposal is to replace the existing external air conditioning unit (Daikin 2MSX50H) with a quieter, more modern external unit (Daikin 3MXM52A); to replace the two existing internal air-conditioning units and to install a new third internal unit in the sitting room of Flat 5 at 19 Buckingham Street.\n \nAlthough 19 Buckingham Street is a Grade II* listed building dating from 1794, the fourth floor on which Flat 5 is located is of modern construction, having been added in the 1980s.\n \nThe proposed replacement unit is quieter and more energy efficient than the existing unit and visually almost identical, apart from minor differences in the manufacturer’s logo and the plastic moulding on the right hand side of the unit. The proposed new unit is slightly larger than the existing one, being 12cm wider and around 20cm taller and longer (detailed comparison table attached). The larger size is indicative of improved sound-proofing and more energy efficient coils within the unit.\n \nThe existing unit is concealed by the walls of the building and a pillar, and is only visible from the fire escape stairwell of the building.\n \nWe are therefore of the view that this change has no effect on the historic nature, character or appearance of the building and that replacing the air conditioning unit in its current location is the least impactful option (rather than, say, building a new enclosure on the flat roof or wall-mounting in a more visible location).\n\nNote that application 26/06435/CLOPUD for a Certificate of Lawful Proposed Use or Development has been submitted on 20th September 2026 to cover the planning aspects of this proposal.",
